<details><summary>Reveal the binomial lower-bound proof</summary>

For natural numbers $b,t,n$, the premise $(b+1)t\le n+1$ implies $b^t\le inom nt$. Induction uses $(t+1) inom n{t+1}=(n-t) inom nt$ and the inequality $b(t+1)\le n-t$. Choosing $b=5$ proves the stated certificate.
